                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/11</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Guatemalan Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Méndez</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-17">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 17, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>The Secretary of State of the United States of America presents his compliments
                    to the Minister of Guatemala, and has the honor to acknowledge the receipt of
                    his memorandum of August 9, which he has read with pleasure, quoting a telegram
                    in which His Excellency the President of Guatemala requests the Minister to
                    approach the Government of the United States and the Latin-American
                    representatives accredited to it, with a view to the proposal by all the nations
                    of the American continent, under the leadership of the United States and at the
                    first favorable opportunity, of the conclusion of the European war.</p>
            </div>
